# Line endings are not cosmetic here.
#
# The repository is developed on Windows, where git's autocrlf turns LF into CRLF on
# checkout. Two of these files are executed by bash inside a Linux container: the
# entrypoint, which is copied into the image, and the probe, which is bind-mounted at
# run time. With CRLF endings the kernel reads the shebang as `/bin/bash\r` and the
# container fails to start, or bash reads every line with a trailing carriage return
# and the probe fails for a reason that has nothing to do with isolation.
#
# A fresh clone on Windows must therefore produce LF for anything a container runs.

* text=auto

*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.mjs         text eol=lf
*.js          text eol=lf
*.json        text eol=lf
*.md          text eol=lf
*.html        text eol=lf
*.css         text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
